# libhrx: stream-carried queue affinity
#
# Backup of uncommitted work in reference/hrx-system, which is gitignored in
# this repo. Apply from the root of an hrx-system checkout:
#     git apply /path/to/hrx-queue-affinity.patch
#
# Base commit: f6ccdeb9ed470bfbf76e132194564bb9afdfde06
#     [Loom] Model checked device execution with kernel launches (#267)
#
# Adds HRX_DEVICE_PROPERTY_QUEUE_COUNT, hrx_stream_create_on_queue() and
# hrx_stream_get_queue_affinity(). Affinity is a bitmask (bit i = queue i);
# zero means any queue, which is what hrx_stream_create() passes, so existing
# callers are unchanged. Out-of-range bits return HRX_STATUS_OUT_OF_RANGE.
#
# CAVEAT: this checkout already carried one unrelated local change before this
# work - a narrowed dispatch-to-dispatch barrier in libhrx/src/libhrx/stream.c
# around lines 468-481. Separate it before upstreaming.

